.TH CHTTPCLIENT_SET_REQUEST_TIMEOUT 3 "2026-10-01" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpclient_set_request_timeout \- set the total request timeout
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpclient.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpclient_set_request_timeout(chttpcli cli, uint64_t us);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function sets the maximum time from the call to chttpclient_do to
the arrival of the last byte of the response body. Give 0 to turn the
timeout off.

chttpclient_do gives ccol_timed_out when a request goes past that
time.

Every tier checks this deadline before each read of the response. Once
it has passed, the request ends with ccol_timed_out, even when the rest
of the response has already arrived and one more read would complete
it, while a response that the client finished reading before the
deadline passed is a success. chttpclient_do, chttpclient_do_async and
chttpclient_do_pooled, and their streaming forms, give the same result
for the same timeline.

Every value other than 0 is honoured as a limit, however far away it
lies: a value too large for the clock to reach, such as UINT64_MAX,
saturates to the latest deadline that the clock can hold, and never
wraps into the past.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cli   The client handle. It must not be CHTTPCLI_INVALID.
us    The timeout in microseconds. 0 means no timeout.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success      The client has the new timeout.
ccol_invalid_args cli is CHTTPCLI_INVALID, or a stale handle of a
                  client that is already destroyed.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpclient_set_connect_timeout (3),
.BR chttpclient_set_max_response_body_size (3),
.BR chttpclient_do (3)
